"""Build the research page from the verified witnesses and exclusion reports."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,html

here=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
states=json.loads((here/'states.json').read_text())['states']
for sub in ('n21-t6','n22-t6','n22-t7'):
    report=json.loads((here/sub/'independent-verification.json').read_text())
    assert report['passed'] and report['arbitraryComplexStatesCovered']
def math(tex,display=False):
    return '<span class="math'+(' display' if display else '')+'" data-tex="'+html.escape(tex,quote=True)+'">'+html.escape(tex)+'</span>'
parts=['''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>21 and 22 qubits · Exact AC states and bounds</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../styles.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><script src="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js" defer></script><style>main{max-width:1050px;padding-block:40px}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,5vw,48px)}h2{margin-top:34px}.display{display:block;overflow-x:auto;padding:12px 0}.links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:16px;margin-block:20px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}th,td{text-align:left;padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.claim{padding:18px 22px;background:var(--paper-alt,#f0efe9);border-left:3px solid var(--accent,#5e4b7c)}</style></head><body><main><a href="../../index.html">← Pure AC-state catalogue</a><p class="eyebrow">Analytical attainment · Exact exclusions</p><h1>Twenty-one and twenty-two qubits</h1><p class="claim">Two compact radical states prove exact attainment of the reported orders. Exact positivity certificates improve the upper bounds. The maximum order is proved at N=22. Fifth-order existence at N=21 remains unresolved.</p><table><thead><tr><th>N</th><th>Exact attained order</th><th>Rigorous maximum-order range</th><th>Remaining question</th></tr></thead><tbody>''']
for n,t,question in [(21,4,'Can a fifth-order state exist?'),(22,5,'Settled: maximum order five.')]:
    parts.append(f'<tr><th>{n}</th><td>{t}</td><td>'+math(rf'{t}\le t_{{\max}}({n})\le {t+1}' if n==21 else r't_{\max}(22)=5')+f'</td><td>{question}</td></tr>')
parts.append('</tbody></table><p>At N=21 the maximum-order conjecture remains four. At N=22 the conjectured fifth-order maximum is now proved. No failed numerical search is used as a nonexistence proof.</p>')
for state in states:
    n,t=state['n'],state['achievedOrder'];w=state['verification']['nextOrderWitness']
    parts.append(f'<section id="n{n}"><h2>{n} qubits: an exactly {t}-AC state</h2>'+math(r'|\psi_{'+str(n)+r'}\rangle='+state['stateLatex'],True))
    parts.append('<p>All Dicke states are normalized. Exact symbolic partial traces give '+math(rf'\rho_q=I_{{q+1}}/(q+1)\quad(1\le q\le {t})')+'. The next reduction is not scalar; for example,</p>'+math(rf'(\rho_{{{t+1}}}-I_{{{t+2}}}/{t+2})_{{{w["row"]},{w["column"]}}}='+w['differenceLatex']+r'\ne0',True))
    if n==21:
        parts.append('<p>The probabilities on the reflected pairs of Dicke indices '+math(r'(0,21),(4,17),(8,13)')+' match the uniform spin moments through degree four. The relative minus sign at index 17 cancels the fourth off-diagonal coherences pairwise; all smaller nonzero shifts are absent from the support.</p>')
    else:
        parts.append('<p>The probabilities '+math(r'(99,154,119,154,99)/625')+' on indices '+math(r'(1,6,11,16,21)')+' match the uniform spin moments through degree five. Reflection makes the odd diagonal moments vanish, and the relative minus sign at index 16 cancels the fifth off-diagonal coherences pairwise.</p><p>This also settles the maximum fifth-order subspace dimension: '+math(r'K(22,5)=1')+'. The state spans an AC line, and the general rectangular-tensor bound gives '+math(r'K(22,5)\le\lfloor22/12\rfloor=1')+'. The independent four-copy certificate below additionally excludes sixth-order pure states, proving that this state has globally maximum AC order five.</p>')
    parts.append(f'<p><a href="../../index.html#n={n}&amp;t={t}&amp;state={state["id"]}">Open this state and its Majorana sphere ↗</a></p></section>')
parts.append('<div class="links"><a href="states.json">Exact Dicke components ↓</a><a href="witnesses.tex">Analytical witness derivation ↓</a><a href="build_witnesses.py">Reproduce the constructions ↓</a><a href="verify_witnesses.py">Independent exact witness verifier ↓</a><a href="independent-verification.json">Witness verification report ↓</a></div>')
parts.append('<h2>Universal upper bounds</h2><p>The exclusions apply to every complex symmetric pure state, without fixing its support or symmetry. For a hypothetical state, average three copies of its projector for the 21-qubit proof, or four copies for the 22-qubit proof, over collective rotations to form a positive operator '+math(r'X')+' of trace one. Anticoherence makes its low-multipole contractions vanish. In invariant block coordinates an exact rational identity has the form</p>'+math(r'-\operatorname{Tr}X=\sum_i y_i R_i(X)+\sum_J\operatorname{Tr}(C_Jx_J)+\sum_L\operatorname{Tr}(Q_LY_L)',True)+'<p>Here '+math(r'R_i(X)=0')+', '+math(r'x_J\succeq0')+' and every certificate matrix is positive definite. The last sum is needed only for the 21-qubit proof: '+math(r'Y_L')+' are positive compressions of the partial time reversal of '+math(r'X')+'. Positivity follows because the rotational average of tensor-power projectors is separable across the first copy and the other two. Thus the right side is nonnegative while the left side is −1, a contradiction.</p>')
for n,t,sub,label in [(21,6,'n21-t6','Three-copy partial-transpose certificate'),(22,6,'n22-t6','Four-copy positivity certificate')]:
    parts.append(f'<h3 id="exclude-n{n}">{n} qubits: no order {t} or higher</h3><p>{label}. The independent verifier uses only Python’s standard library and reconstructs the physical representation, all selected contraction equations and the rational positive-matrix factorizations. It does not import the numerical discovery calculation.</p><div class="links">'+''.join(f'<a href="{sub}/{file}">{text} ↓</a>' for file,text in [('proof.tex','Complete LaTeX proof'),('certificate.json','Exact rational certificate'),('verify_independently.py','Independent verifier'),('independent-verification.json','Exact verification report')])+'</div>')
parts.append('''<h2>What is not proved</h2><p>Exact attainment by these particular states does not establish that their orders are globally maximal. The remaining question is fifth-order existence at N=21. The tested three-copy and four-copy positivity relaxations did not exclude it; this is not an existence result for pure states. The catalogue keeps this question unresolved. The finite searches and relaxation tests are documented in the <a href="n21-t5-search-report.json">research report</a>. An additional independently verified <a href="n22-t7/proof.tex">three-copy seventh-order exclusion at N=22</a> is retained as an auxiliary certificate; the stronger sixth-order exclusion proves the maximum.</p></main><script>document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded',()=>{for(const el of document.querySelectorAll('[data-tex]'))katex.render(el.dataset.tex,el,{displayMode:el.classList.contains('display'),throwOnError:true});});</script></body></html>''')
(here/'index.html').write_text(''.join(parts))
